#: ../../export.rst:5
msgid "Marquetry can persist a trained model in three ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export.rst:7
msgid ""
":func:`marquetry.onnx_export.export_onnx` -- export the traced inference "
"graph as an **ONNX** model which runs anywhere ONNX Runtime works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export.rst:10
msgid ""
":func:`marquetry.model_archive.save_archive` -- save the graph and the "
"weights together as a **marquetry archive** (``.mq``). The archive can be"
" loaded back with :func:`marquetry.model_archive.load_archive` without "
"the original model class, and the restored model stays trainable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export.rst:14
msgid ""
":meth:`marquetry.Layer.save_params` -- plain npz weight checkpoints "
"(weights only; you need the original model class to restore them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export.rst:17
msgid ""
"Both exporters trace the model by running one forward pass with sample "
"inputs in test mode, so the exported graph reflects the inference "
"behavior (e.g. dropout is excluded)."
msgstr ""

